notes='Author page1, archive foot363, begins Formule de Decalage (Quillen - Bousfield), with an Illusie thesis reference. It has a cancelled F, two extensively slashed trial formulas, and a densely crossed third trial; these are not live assertions. The first cancelled symmetric power remains j or i, whereas the other three powers read j. A short M-to-M margin diagram has curved underbraces. The K-to-E-to-K diagram has a headless vertical stroke. The inserted tensor expression uses Phi; an apparent subscript of E is only a thickening on the opening parenthesis. Three Koszul-like sequences follow, the first two ending in0 and the third unfinished. In the third sequence the exterior exponent is visibly i, although a homogeneous degree-i sequence would require1: the displayed Gamma^(i-1) factor tensor Lambda^i has total polynomial degree2i-1, which equals i only when i=1. The ink therefore remains Lambda^i. The boxed formula has r and r-i, a short underline and a possible question mark against the border. Its i=1 specialization is degree-consistent with N K(M,n)=M[n]: both sides are supported at r=n+1 under the usual homological indexing. This limited check neither proves the decalage isomorphism nor establishes the sequences exact without additional assumptions. Three bottom formulas shift X by1 and2 and put -i or -2i on the right; the first has a deleted -i in the L subscript. No shift convention is supplied explicitly. No date.'
